#====================================================================
# E219 — Complete an OHOS Meson cross file on a Windows build host
#====================================================================

id:                     E296
trigger_tool:           conan|meson|clang
phase:                  configuration|linking
error_signature:        prefix value 'C:/' must be an absolute path|Unable to detect linker.*program not executable|Target: x86_64-w64-windows-gnu

severity:               2
category:               build-system|meson|cross-build|windows
match_keywords:         Conan, MesonToolchain, Windows, OHOS, cross file, C:/, prefix, target, sysroot, llvm-ar.exe, linker, program not executable
title:                  Complete an OHOS Meson cross file on a Windows build host

root_cause:             Conan's Meson helper derives the install prefix from the Windows build machine, while Meson validates it for the POSIX OHOS target. A CMake-only OHOS user toolchain is not consumed by Meson, so compiler paths alone retain the SDK clang default x86_64-w64-windows-gnu target and omit the OHOS sysroot and Windows-suffixed LLVM archiver tools.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 Meson recipes cross-built from Windows to OHOS armv8 with SDK clang; especially profiles that configure tools.cmake.cmaketoolchain:user_toolchain but only provide c/cpp paths to tools.build:compiler_executables.
verification_cmd:       inspect conan_meson_cross.ini for prefix '/', --target=aarch64-linux-ohos, native/sysroot, llvm-ar.exe and llvm-ranlib.exe; then force conan create --build=<package>/*

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           complete-meson-cross-machine
rec_description:        Use a POSIX target prefix with Meson install staging, derive the SDK sysroot from the structured compiler path, add the OHOS target and sysroot to compile/link args, and inject absolute ar/ranlib paths into the generated Meson cross file.
rec_command:            set Meson prefix to /; extend MesonToolchain c_args/cpp_args/c_link_args/cpp_link_args with --target=aarch64-linux-ohos and --sysroot=<sdk>/native/sysroot; set ar and ranlib from the SDK llvm/bin directory
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      dedicated-meson-profile
fallback_description:   Put the same target, sysroot, prefix, and LLVM binary declarations in a project-owned Meson machine file and reference it through tools.meson.mesontoolchain:extra_machine_files.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          meson-machine-file

forbid_1_pattern:       tools.cmake.cmaketoolchain:user_toolchain.*MesonToolchain
forbid_1_reason:        Meson does not load a CMake user toolchain; compiler paths without target/sysroot silently describe the Windows host compiler target.
forbid_1_consequence:   Meson rejects the linker or produces host-targeted probes instead of OHOS objects.

forbid_2_pattern:       prefix=C:/.*host_machine.*harmonyos
forbid_2_reason:        A Windows drive prefix is a build-host path, not the POSIX target prefix used with Meson destdir staging.
forbid_2_consequence:   Meson setup fails before compilation or installs target paths with host semantics.

